06:59.660 --> 07:03.020
an airport called South End,
which is a mid-sized field.

07:03.020 --> 07:05.940
They take heavy metal there as
well.

07:05.940 --> 07:09.500
And I knew the captain Dan
wouldn't be able to fly

07:09.500 --> 07:11.580
safety pilot with me on Sunday.

07:11.580 --> 07:15.220
And I couldn't get Jason, who's
been flying with me before

07:15.220 --> 07:16.820
because he had to work in the
tower.

07:16.820 --> 07:21.060
So I said, you know what, why
don't we alter our flight plan

07:21.060 --> 07:21.780
on the way back?

07:21.780 --> 07:25.180
That's from Antwerp to Farrowks.

07:25.180 --> 07:26.300
We'll stop off at South End.

07:26.300 --> 07:27.940
Then we'll have seen the airport
and I'll feel a little more

07:27.940 --> 07:29.140
confident.

07:29.140 --> 07:30.780
And so we did that and
everything went fine.

07:30.780 --> 07:33.180
And I, oh, man, fucking
impeccable landing.

07:33.180 --> 07:36.380
A greaser as Captain Dan called
it just nice and smooth,

07:36.380 --> 07:38.460
barely felt me touched down.

07:38.460 --> 07:41.820
And I hadn't told Patricia that
I'd actually never

07:41.820 --> 07:44.620
flown solo in this aircraft ever
before.

07:44.620 --> 07:47.620
Well, you know, because the
missions have always been to
Antwerp,

07:47.620 --> 07:50.740
which, as I said, is that a lot
you have to do

07:50.740 --> 07:54.380
as a reasonable amount of work
that has to go on,

07:54.380 --> 07:57.460
particularly communicating with
air traffic control,

07:57.460 --> 08:00.580
that at least six different
people you have to talk to

08:00.580 --> 08:03.220
and watch out for other idiots
who are flying around on the
weekend.

08:03.220 --> 08:06.260
Of course, who don't talk to
anybody and just seem to fly
around

08:06.260 --> 08:08.500
it will.

08:08.500 --> 08:10.500
So it was a beautiful day,
Sunday.

08:10.500 --> 08:16.580
It was about 10 miles per hour
of wind coming just from the
north,

08:16.580 --> 08:17.380
north east.

08:17.380 --> 08:21.300
So actually perfect for South
End because they have a 0, 6,

08:21.300 --> 08:25.420
2, 4 runway so you can literally
fly right in.

08:25.500 --> 08:28.140
And off we went, first time
together,

08:28.140 --> 08:30.740
we've never been in the plane
together alone either.

08:30.740 --> 08:34.220
So of course, we did a little
semi-mile,

08:34.220 --> 08:37.220
mile high club thing at 2,400
feet.

08:37.220 --> 08:38.540
So it didn't really count.

08:38.540 --> 08:42.100
And it was really just a kiss
because damn there's a lot of
work

08:42.100 --> 08:45.260
to do in that continent.

08:45.260 --> 08:48.740
So I flew Patricia out, you
know, great, dropped her off at
South End.

08:48.740 --> 08:49.620
Everything was perfect.

08:49.620 --> 08:52.220
Now on the way back, as I said,
I'd never soloed in this
aircraft

08:52.220 --> 08:54.420
before, of course, I flown solo
because you have to in order

08:54.420 --> 08:59.380
to get your license, but I never
actually landed it with just
myself.

08:59.380 --> 09:02.020
And I didn't really think about
it because, you know,

09:02.020 --> 09:06.020
I guess typically I've always
had minimum of two people and

09:06.020 --> 09:09.580
oftentimes four and it behaves
differently, you know,

09:09.580 --> 09:10.980
because of the way, it's very
obvious.

09:10.980 --> 09:12.900
And it doesn't matter,
Patricia's not heavy,

09:12.900 --> 09:15.940
but you could just put 20 pounds
in the right hand front seat

09:15.940 --> 09:16.900
and it will make a difference.

09:16.900 --> 09:18.980
But I just wasn't thinking of
it.

09:18.980 --> 09:21.700
So I'm coming in for a few,
because I dropped her off,

09:21.700 --> 09:23.460
I was going to fly back to some
grocery shopping

09:23.460 --> 09:25.860
and then go pick her up at the
end of the day.

09:25.860 --> 09:27.700
And I come in for the landing
and everything's perfect.

09:27.700 --> 09:31.700
And all of a sudden, it just
like, because it was so light,

09:31.700 --> 09:33.860
I configured it a little bit
differently.

09:33.860 --> 09:36.020
And I start to bounce and start
to pour up around

09:36.020 --> 09:39.620
and so I call it go around and I
fly around, try to do it again.

09:39.620 --> 09:42.820
Another oscillating bounce,
like, oh, wait a minute.

09:42.820 --> 09:44.020
Of course, I'm much lighter.

09:44.020 --> 09:45.780
So the third time, of course,
being a charm,

09:45.780 --> 09:48.580
and I dropped it onto the
tarmac.

09:48.580 --> 09:50.180
And as you know, as we say in
aviation,

09:50.180 --> 09:53.060
if you walk away from the
landing, it was a fantastic
landing.

09:53.060 --> 09:55.060
But what was really nice is that
Jason, as I said,

09:55.060 --> 09:56.020
he couldn't come flying with me.

09:56.020 --> 09:57.300
He was in the tower.

09:57.300 --> 10:00.020
And so he's, of course, watching
this, you know,

10:00.020 --> 10:03.860
watching me, like a fucking
flipper, a Cirque de Soleil
moves.

10:03.860 --> 10:07.300
They're trying to get the plane
on the landing strip.

10:07.300 --> 10:09.060
And I'm like, oh, Jason, I'm
going around on this one.

10:09.060 --> 10:10.180
He says, oh, it's all right,
man.

10:10.180 --> 10:11.060
And it happens to all of us.

10:11.060 --> 10:12.100
He was really nice.

10:12.100 --> 10:14.020
It was so nice to have that kind
of reassuring,

10:14.020 --> 10:15.300
don't worry about it, dude.

10:15.300 --> 10:16.740
We're not laughing at you here.

10:16.740 --> 10:18.020
And of course, he was laughing
at me,

10:18.020 --> 10:22.420
but at least he wasn't
humiliating me publicly.

10:22.420 --> 10:25.460
And I had kind of neglected to
mention

10:25.460 --> 10:28.100
the Patricia that I'd never
soloed in the aircraft,

10:28.100 --> 10:29.380
but she had a great time.

10:29.380 --> 10:30.500
It was so nice.

10:30.500 --> 10:32.020
You know, so I picked her up and
we flew back

10:32.020 --> 10:36.580
and that whole bit from South
End to about big and hill.

10:36.580 --> 10:38.820
It is, you know, there's
relatively no traffic.

10:38.820 --> 10:40.740
You can see London right off in
the distance

10:40.740 --> 10:42.340
because you're flying over the
Thames

10:42.340 --> 10:43.940
at the last bit of the Thames
there.

10:43.940 --> 10:45.620
It's completely smooth air.

10:45.620 --> 10:46.580
It was just wonderful.

10:46.580 --> 10:51.220
And we had a great time and
landed without bouncing.

10:51.220 --> 10:53.380
You know, one of Adam's typical
plump were downlandings,

10:53.380 --> 10:54.820
but it was without bouncing.

10:54.820 --> 10:56.820
I just, I did call to the tower
and said, Jason,

10:56.820 --> 11:00.180
I might wheel still on and said,
yeah, we either still there.

11:00.180 --> 11:02.740
